 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "JavaScript Assignment"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript Assignment Operators"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Assignment operators assign values to JavaScript variables."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Given that x = 10 and y = 5, the table below explains the assignment operators:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Operator",
    "Example",
    "Same As",
    "Result"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "=",
     "x = y",
     "x = y",
     "x = 5"
    ],
    [
     "+=",
     "x += y",
     "x = x + y",
     "x = 15"
    ],
    [
     "-=",
     "x -= y",
     "x = x - y",
     "x = 5"
    ],
    [
     "*=",
     "x *= y",
     "x = x * y",
     "x = 50"
    ],
    [
     "**=",
     "x **= y",
     "x = x ** y",
     "x = 100000"
    ],
    [
     "/=",
     "x /= y",
     "x = x / y",
     "x = 2"
    ],
    [
     "%=",
     "x %= y",
     "x = x % y",
     "x = 0"
    ],
    [
     ":",
     "x: 45",
     "size.x = 45",
     "x = 45"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Logical Assignment Operators"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Operator",
    "Example",
    "Result"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "&&=",
     "true &&= 10",
     "x = 10"
    ],
    [
     "||=",
     "false ||= 10",
     "x = 10"
    ],
    [
     "??=",
     "null ??= 10",
     "x = 10"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The = Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Simple Assignment Operator assigns a simple value to a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;",
   "caption": "Simple Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10 + y;",
   "caption": "Simple Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_equal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The += Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Addition Assignment Operator adds a value to a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\nx += 5;",
   "caption": "Addition Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_plusequal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The -= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Subtraction Assignment Operator subtracts a value from a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\n\nx -= 5;",
   "caption": "Subtraction Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_minequal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The *= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Multiplication Assignment Operator multiplies a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\nx *= 5;",
   "caption": "Multiplication Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_multequal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The **= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Exponentiation Assignment Operator raises a variable to the power of the operand."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\n\nx **= 5;",
   "caption": "Exponentiation Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_exponential"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The /= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Division Assignment Operator divides a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\nx /= 5;",
   "caption": "Division Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_divequal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The %= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Remainder Assignment Operator assigns a remainder to a variable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\n\nx %= 5;",
   "caption": "Remainder Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_modequal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "String Assignment"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Two assignment operators can assign values to strings:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Simple Assignment Operator assigns a simple value to a string."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Addition Assignment Operator adds a value to a string."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The = Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Simple Assignment Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Hello\";",
   "caption": "String Assignment"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_equal3"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The += Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Addition Assignment Operator Can also be used to add strings."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Hello\";\ntext += \" World\";",
   "caption": "Addition Assignment Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_plusequal2"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The &&= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Logical AND assignment operator is used between two values."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If the first value is true, the second value is assigned."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = true;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = false;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 1;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 0;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = undefined;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = null;\n\nlet y = x &&= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical AND Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_logical_and_and"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The &&= operator is an ES2020 feature."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The ||= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Logical OR assignment operator is used between two values."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If the first value is false, the second value is assigned."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = false;\n\nlet y = x ||= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical OR Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = true;\n\nlet y = x ||= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical OR Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = null;\n\nlet y = x ||= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical OR Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = undefined;\n\nlet y = x ||= 10;",
   "caption": "Logical OR Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_logical_or_or"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The ||= operator is an ES2020 feature."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The ??= Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Nullish coalescing assignment operator is used between two values."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If the first value is undefined or null, the second value is assigned."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x;\n\nx ??= 10;",
   "caption": "Nullish Coalescing Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 0;\n\nx ??= 10;",
   "caption": "Nullish Coalescing Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = null;\n\nx ??= 10;",
   "caption": "Nullish Coalescing Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = undefined;\n\nx ??= 10;",
   "caption": "Nullish Coalescing Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 10;\n\nlet y = 5;\n\nx ??= 10;",
   "caption": "Nullish Coalescing Assignment Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_assign_nullish"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The ??= operator is an ES2020 feature."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Quick Reference"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Operator",
     "Result"
    ],
    [
     "x &&= y",
     "Assigns y to x only if x is truthy"
    ],
    [
     "x ||= y",
     "Assigns y to x only if x is falsy"
    ],
    [
     "x ??= y",
     "Assigns y to x only if x is null or undefined"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The 8 FALSY Values"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "false",
     "The boolean keyword itself"
    ],
    [
     "0",
     "The number zero"
    ],
    [
     "-0",
     "Negative zero"
    ],
    [
     "0n",
     "BigInt zero"
    ],
    [
     "\"\", '', ``",
     "Any empty string"
    ],
    [
     "null",
     "The absence of any value"
    ],
    [
     "undefined",
     "A variable that has not been assigned a value"
    ],
    [
     "NaN",
     "\"Not-a-Number,\" usually the result of an invalid math operation"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "These are TRUTHY"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It is a common mistake to think these are falsy, but they actually evaluate to true:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "\"0\"",
     "A string containing a zero is truthy because it is not empty"
    ],
    [
     "\"false\"",
     "The string \"false\" is truthy"
    ],
    [
     "[ ]",
     "An empty array is truthy"
    ],
    [
     "{ }",
     "An empty object is truthy"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The Spread (...) Operator"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The ... operator splits iterables into individual elements."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"12345\";\n\nlet min = Math.min(...text);\n\nlet max = Math.max(...text);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
